The store of TestRetire, deployed in us-east-1 and us-west-2, and under want/ what each
case prints and the dynaflux.lock it leaves (go test -update rewrites them). The test
generates the project with page_counts_v1.sql as dynaflux/page_counts.sql, then with
page_counts_v2.sql, so page_counts@v2 is current and page_counts@v1 retained.
-- dynaflux.yaml --
store: shop
regions: [us-east-1, us-west-2]
-- dynaflux/page_views.sql --
CREATE STREAM page_views (user_id String, page String)
PRIMARY KEY (user_id);
-- page_counts_v1.sql --
CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW page_counts
ORDER BY (page)
AS SELECT page, count() AS views
FROM page_views
GROUP BY page;
-- page_counts_v2.sql --
CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW page_counts
ORDER BY (page)
AS SELECT page, count() AS views, max(user_id) AS last_user
FROM page_views
GROUP BY page;
-- want/already_retired_skips_the_checks.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
retire can't see application builds or query.yaml stacks: one older than the deployed catalog may still query page_counts@v1, and gets ErrViewNotReady, or answers 503, once it is retired. Deploy the application and query.yaml first.
-- want/already_retired_skips_the_checks.stdout --
page_counts@v1:
  us-east-1      retire   live
  us-west-2      none     already retired
  dynaflux.lock  retire   retained
us-east-1: page_counts@v1 retired

Checked prefix (none) in us-east-1, us-west-2.
dynaflux.lock: page_counts@v1 retired
Next: run dynaflux generate, and deploy regional.yaml in every region, which deletes the table of page_counts@v1.
Before you deploy another environment with this dynaflux.lock, run dynaflux retire page_counts@v1 -prefix <its prefix> there, with its credentials.
-- want/broken_version.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
retire can't see application builds or query.yaml stacks: one older than the deployed catalog may still query page_counts@v1, and gets ErrViewNotReady, or answers 503, once it is retired. Deploy the application and query.yaml first.
