  us-east-1      retire   live
  us-west-2      retire   broken
  dynaflux.lock  retire   retained
us-east-1: page_counts@v1 retired
us-west-2: page_counts@v1 retired

Checked prefix (none) in us-east-1, us-west-2.
dynaflux.lock: page_counts@v1 retired
Next: run dynaflux generate, and deploy regional.yaml in every region, which deletes the table of page_counts@v1.
Before you deploy another environment with this dynaflux.lock, run dynaflux retire page_counts@v1 -prefix <its prefix> there, with its credentials.
-- want/current_broken.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
us-west-2: error DF7303: page_counts@v2, the view's current version in the deployed catalog, is broken in us-west-2
  hint: rebuild it first with dynaflux generate -rebuild page_counts, then deploy and backfill the new version
-- want/current_broken.stdout --
page_counts@v1:
  us-east-1      retire   live
  us-west-2      refused  pending_backfill
  dynaflux.lock  retire   retained
-- want/current_in_the_lock.stderr --
dynaflux.lock:1:1: error DF7301: page_counts@v2 is the current version of page_counts in dynaflux.lock
  hint: make another version current, or remove the view's SQL, and run dynaflux generate
-- want/current_in_the_lock.stdout --
-- want/current_not_live.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
us-west-2: error DF7303: page_counts@v2, the view's current version in the deployed catalog, is pending_backfill in us-west-2
  hint: fill it first: dynaflux backfill page_counts@v2 -region us-west-2
-- want/current_not_live.stdout --
page_counts@v1:
  us-east-1      retire   live
  us-west-2      refused  pending_backfill
  dynaflux.lock  retire   retained
